ppened to his mother was actually  pretty tragic  in the 1940s Walt Disney bought a house  for his parents he had obviously come  into some money and wanted to share the  wealth with his parents when they moved  in the furnace was on the fritz Walt had  some people from his studio go to the  house and fix the furnace unfortunately  the furnace continued to leak when the  housekeeper came in one more  she had to pull his mother and father  out of the home Walt's mother passed  away from this incident and his father  ended up in the hospital everyone who  knew wall around this time said that he  never spoke about what happened to his  parents he completely felt responsible  even though it wasn't necessarily his  fault he had tried to do something nice  for his parents and unfortunately it  didn't turn out well the studio workers  who went to the house to fix the furnace  weren't trained on how to do it and  didn't know what they were doing many  people say that Walt was haunted by the  incident because of this it may have  been too painful for him to include  mothers in his movies or to focus on  mother child relationships at all  instead he preferred to completely keep  mothers out of his film another theory  focuses on how Disney movies tend to be  coming-of-age stories we follow most of  the princesses as they grow up and come  into their own  why Erik run away with you this theory  says that a child is never an adult  until they assume the role that their  parents would normally take by not  giving the characters mother figures  Walt set them to grow up right before  our eyes  this theory is a lot less bleak than the  first one so we won't blame you if this  is the one that you want to believe this  theme has been showcased in lots of  movies and shows even outside of the  Disney World from Harry Potter to Game  of Thrones this idea is one that is  quite popular our next theory is also  much lighter than the first two  another common thread between all of the  Disney Princesses is that they make  mistakes they stumble and fall through  most of the beginning of their stories  in order to have a triumphant victory by  the end without their initial mistakes  there would hardly be any story to tell  well some people believe that if Walt  had given each of these girls mothers  they wouldn't have made half as many  mistakes as they did think about it when  you're headed down the wrong path and  about to make a huge error who's the one  that usually puts you back on track your  mom right moms have a weird sixth sense  about these things  so if a mom had been there to tell Ariel  not to trade her voice and soul to an  evil witch just staying out with a boy  there wouldn't have been a film if  Cinderella's mom had been there then  there would not have been an evil  stepmother in her life and no reason for  her to go to the ball it's no  White's mother had been around she never  would have had to flee the castle and  never would have met those Seven Dwarfs  basically the mothers would have ruined  the stories there just wasn't a place  for them to fit in now there are a few  exceptions to this role Merida and  Rapunzel Merida's relationship with her  mother is kind of the center of brave  Rapunzel's relationship with her  stepmother is also the center of tangled  but each of these relationships isn't  exactly healthy in brave Merida's mom  wants her to be something other than  what she is her mom spent the whole  first portion of the movie trying to  force Merida to change everything we  never had I asked you what do you expect  us to do sure the to do mend their  relationship throughout the film but we  can definitely tell that Merida and her  mom were at odds for most of her life  the relationship between Rapunzel and  her mom is even weirder first of all the  lady in the film is not actually  Rapunzel's mom at all but actually a  witch who pretty much kidnaps Rapunzel  when she's a baby she then hides  Rapunzel in a tower where she obsesses  over her and tells her how great she is  but doesn't let her leave it's a really  sick relationship so even the princesses  who do have mothers don't have the best  relationships with them which makes it  extremely clear that something was up  with Walt and his ideas of motherhood we  wonder if the new generation of Disney  movies and princesses will keep up this  theme or if modern times will force  Disney to start adding mothers into the  films what do you think and that's it  for the sad reason why all Disney  Princesses don't have a mom which theory  do you believe let us know in the  comments below see you next time  [Music]

